To complete this S3 migration task using AWS CLI, follow these steps:

1. Create the new private S3 bucket
First, create the bucket:

aws s3api create-bucket \
  --bucket datacenter-sync-32402 \
  --region <your-region>

Replace <your-region> with the AWS region where the bucket should be created (for example, us-east-1 or ap-south-1).

For regions other than us-east-1, include the location constraint:

aws s3api create-bucket \
  --bucket datacenter-sync-32402 \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=ap-south-1

2. Verify the new bucket is private
S3 buckets are private by default, but confirm the ACL:

aws s3api get-bucket-acl \
  --bucket datacenter-sync-32402

You should see that only the bucket owner has full control.

Also verify public access blocks:

aws s3api get-public-access-block \
  --bucket datacenter-sync-32402

If not configured, enable them:

aws s3api put-public-access-block \
  --bucket datacenter-sync-32402 \
  --public-access-block-configuration \
  BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true

3. Sync data from the existing bucket to the new bucket
Use AWS CLI s3 sync:

aws s3 sync \
  s3://datacenter-s3-9789 \
  s3://datacenter-sync-32402

This will:

Copy all objects from the source bucket
Preserve directory structure
Copy only missing or changed objects
Maintain metadata where supported
For large migrations, you can enable progress output:

aws s3 sync \
  s3://datacenter-s3-9789 \
  s3://datacenter-sync-32402 \
  --only-show-errors

4. Verify object counts
Count objects in both buckets:

aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-s3-9789 --recursive | wc -l

and:

aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-sync-32402 --recursive | wc -l

The counts should match.

5. Verify data consistency
Run a dry-run sync to confirm nothing remains to copy:

aws s3 sync \
  s3://datacenter-s3-9789 \
  s3://datacenter-sync-32402 \
  --dryrun

If the migration is complete, this command should return no files.

6. Optional: Compare object listings
Generate object inventories:

aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-s3-9789 --recursive > source-list.txt

aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-sync-32402 --recursive > destination-list.txt

Compare them:

diff source-list.txt destination-list.txt

No output means the object lists match.

7. Final verification checklist
✅ Bucket datacenter-sync-32402 created
✅ Bucket is private
✅ All objects copied from datacenter-s3-9789
✅ Object counts match
✅ aws s3 sync --dryrun shows no pending transfers
✅ Object listings match

